{"node_id": "real_068_batch_63_NIHMLPFall2021_17_HY_002", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0003"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0003_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "One recent study, led by Rachel Hardeman, Ph.D., looked\nat whether women had worse birth outcomes following\nevents in Minneapolis, Minnesota in 2020. More than half of\nthe women studied reported feeling like the events affected\ntheir current pregnancy. Later, nearly 60% of those women\ngave birth to preterm babies who were underweight or died.", "semantic_text": "One recent study, led by Rachel Hardeman, Ph.D., looked at whether women had worse birth outcomes following events in Minneapolis, Minnesota in 2020. More than half of the women studied reported feeling like the events affected their current pregnancy. Later, nearly 60% of those women gave birth to preterm babies who were underweight or died.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0003_geometry", "bbox": [103, 283, 607, 433], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0003"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_snapshot_non_nasa_20261118_2243_v2/batch_25/hybrid/real_068_batch_63_NIHMLPFall2021/page_0017/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "real_068_batch_63_NIHMLPFall2021_17_HY_003", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0004", "D0005"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0004_F001", "D0005_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Another recent study, led by Maeve Wallace, Ph.D.,\nlooked at nonpregnancy-related causes of death during\npregnancy and the year after birth in Louisiana. Of the\n119 pregnancy-associated deaths during 2016 and 2017,\n13% were homicides. Researchers estimated that for every\n100,000 women who were pregnant or postpartum,\nthere were 13 homicide deaths. This outnumbered deaths\nfrom any single obstetric cause, including blood pressure\ndisorders and amniotic fluid entering the blood.", "semantic_text": "Another recent study, led by Maeve Wallace, Ph.D., looked at nonpregnancy-related causes of death during pregnancy and the year after birth in Louisiana. Of the 119 pregnancy-associated deaths during 2016 and 2017,\n13% were homicides. Researchers estimated that for every 100,000 women who were pregnant or postpartum, there were 13 homicide deaths. This outnumbered deaths from any single obstetric cause, including blood pressure disorders and amniotic fluid entering the blood.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0004_geometry", "bbox": [103, 433, 572, 534], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0004"}, {"member_id": "D0005_geometry", "bbox": [639, 232, 1131, 357], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0005"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_snapshot_non_nasa_20261118_2243_v2/batch_25/hybrid/real_068_batch_63_NI